# =============================================================================
# geometry/iceslab/iceslab_2D_L1mm_eps20um_keff.opts — analytic benchmark for k_eff
# homogenization (-keff). NOT a physics run.
#
# A 50/50 ice/air layered medium: ice on [0, Ly/2], air above. For layered
# two-phase media the effective conductivity is known in closed form, so this
# is the gate that says the cell problem is solving the right equations at all.
# With k_ice = 2.29 and k_air = 0.02 W/m/K:
#
#   k_00  (parallel to the layers, arithmetic mean)  = 1.155000     W/m/K
#   k_11  (perpendicular, harmonic mean)             = 0.0396538    W/m/K
#   k_01, k_10                                       = 0
#
# k_00 is insensitive to eps: the arithmetic mean depends only on the mean ice
# fraction, which the CONTINUOUS profile makes exactly 0.5 for any eps (see the
# long comment on FormInitialIceSlab2D in src/initial_conditions.c).
#
# COMPARE AGAINST THE MEASURED VOLUME FRACTION, NOT AGAINST 0.5, so that any
# error in how the IC represents the slab is divided out. Until 2026-09-23 the
# measured TOT_ICE was 5.002e-07 against an exact 5.000e-07 at Nx=Ny=256 (4e-4
# relative). That was not spline error, as this header used to say:
# IC_COORD_UNIFORM stretched periodic ICs by (N+1)/N, giving
# phi_bar - 1/2 = 0.0485/N exactly (now fixed in FillIC2D). Evaluate the
# analytic forms at the measured phi_bar, which the k_eff CSV reports in its
# own column:
#
#   k_parallel = phi*k_ice + (1-phi)*k_air
#   k_perp     = 1/( phi/k_ice + (1-phi)/k_air )
#
# That isolates what this benchmark is actually for -- whether the cell problem
# is solved correctly -- from how well the IC discretises a step function.
#
# k_11 IS eps-sensitive, and converges to the harmonic mean FROM ABOVE: the
# diffuse band is a high-conductivity short circuit across what is otherwise a
# series resistance, so a wider interface reads high.
#
# THE DRIFT NOW HAS A CLOSED FORM. An earlier version of this header said the
# eps bias "has no analytic value to compare against". It does. To first order
# the band acts as a sharp interface carrying two Gibbs surface excesses, and
# both are exactly computable for the logistic profile:
#
#   tangential (conductance)  Sigma_t = 0                       <- exactly zero
#   normal     (resistance)   Sigma_n = -eps*(1/k_a - 1/k_i)*ln(k_i/k_a)
#
# Sigma_t = 0 is why k_00 is eps-insensitive, noted empirically above; it holds
# because the logistic profile is antisymmetric, so the arithmetic law moves no
# ice across the interface. Sigma_n is nonzero because 1/K is convex in phi.
# Hence, with n_Gamma = 2 interfaces per period,
#
#   <1/K>(eps) = [phi/k_i + (1-phi)/k_a] - (n_Gamma*eps/Ly)*(1/k_a - 1/k_i)*ln(k_i/k_a)
#   k_11(eps)  = 1/<1/K>(eps)
#
# At k_i/k_a = 2.29/0.02 the constant is 234.959 m K/W, giving +17.0% bias at
# eps = Ly/128 and +3.8% at Ly/512. Derivation: sections 6-7 of
# projects/effective_thermal_cond/docs/calonne_to_phasefield_equivalence.tex.
#
# -periodic 1 is MANDATORY (the solver errors out otherwise). It also means the
# slab has TWO interfaces: y = Ly/2 and the y = 0 == Ly seam. Both are real and
# both must be resolved. That is the n_Gamma = 2 above.
#
# Run it with -keff_only, which takes one sample from the IC and exits. Go
# through the run script, not the binary:
#
#   ./scripts/Studio/run_enceladus.sh iceslab_2D_L1mm_eps20um_keff \
#       snow_T-20_h1.00_1d keff -- -keff 1 -keff_only 1 \
#       -keff_ksp_type preonly -keff_pc_type lu
#
# eps ladder: DO NOT run it at fixed resolution. The previous instruction here
# ("-eps 1.5625e-5 / 7.8125e-6 / 3.90625e-6 at -Nx 1024 -Ny 1024") confounds the
# interface bias with ordinary mesh convergence, because elements-per-band
# changes by 4x down the ladder. Scale Ny with eps to hold eps/dy fixed at the
# 5.12 of this file's reference point. The committed driver does exactly that:
#
#   ./studies/keff_sharp_limit/verification/verify_keff_sharp_limit.sh
#
# Use CG+GAMG above ~256^2; a direct LU factorization stops being comfortable
# there.
# =============================================================================

-ic_type ice_slab
-dim 2

-Lx 1.0e-3
-Ly 1.0e-3
-Nx 256
-Ny 256

-p 2
-C 1
-periodic 1                       # REQUIRED by -keff; also creates the y=0 seam interface

-eps 2.0e-5                       # ~7.8 elements across the phi=0.05..0.95 band at Ny=256
-eps_temp_override 1              # eps here is chosen for resolution, not from comp_eps.py

-delt_t 1.0e-4
